    "created_at": "2021-07-29T08:53:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-29T08:53:23Z",
    "body": "That would mean you'd always have to invoke fetch from an event loop thread, right? I'm not sure that works for Background Fetch. And it would also require restructuring other existing callers, though that is needed either way to be fair.\r\n\r\nAnd it would mean you'd have to queue a task to resume the fetch algorithm (to deal with redirects and such) which I guess could work, but it seems like a pretty large undertaking.",
